2026-05-09 16:31:08,329 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:31:08,329 - INFO - **Your friend has a point that:** The complete replacement faces real challenges—energy storage technology, grid infrastructure, intermittency issues, and the energy demands of modern society all require solutions we're still developing. Some sectors (like aviation and heavy industry) remain particularly difficult to fully decarbonize with current renewable technology.
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - **The honest answer:** Renewables *can* replace fossil fuels, but it depends on:
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - - How quickly technology advances
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - - Investment levels and political will
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - - Whether we also pursue energy efficiency and other solutions (nuclear, carbon capture, etc.)
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - - What timeline we're discussing
2026-05-09 16:31:08,330 - INFO - 
